# Where the client sends API calls. **Keep it relative.**
#
# The refresh token is an HttpOnly cookie scoped to `/api/v1/auth` and marked
# `SameSite=Lax`, which a browser will not send on a cross-site request at all —
# so a client pointed at a different origin than the API loses every session at
# the first token refresh, fifteen minutes in, with nothing but a 401 to show
# for it. One origin is a requirement, not a preference: `apps/api` refuses to
# start in production when `API_BASE_URL` and `WEB_BASE_URL` disagree.
#
# Both environments arrange that the same way. In development the Vite dev
# server proxies `/api` to the API process (see vite.config.ts); in production
# the `web` service in `docker-compose.deploy.yml` is an nginx that serves this
# bundle and proxies `/api` to the API container.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# Only used by the dev proxy. Change if the API is not on port 4000.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4000
